{
  "slug": "rasid-web-system",
  "projectSlug": "rasid",
  "title": "Web-system",
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "px8dge5v",
      "title": "The exercise",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "3e2q930o",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "ic6qno1z",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "A product, start to finish"
              },
              {
                "id": "gvsebg71",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "I set myself a challenge: design a complete fintech experience, from the login flow to a full money dashboard, with no brief and no client."
              },
              {
                "id": "u49byju6",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "The goal was not a single pretty screen. It was to build a real product as a system, in both light and dark, over a couple of focused days, and to see if I could keep it consistent all the way through. The idea behind it was simple: every riyal, in view."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "flag"
    },
    {
      "id": "6cf2hem5",
      "title": "The direction",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "fd9wdjix",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "1bqkmkcb",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "Calm, with one green"
              },
              {
                "id": "77ps27r7",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Money apps carry a lot of anxiety, so I designed against it. Near neutral surfaces, generous space, and clear hierarchy keep the screen calm, and a single emerald green carries action and positive movement and nothing else."
              },
              {
                "id": "iuoe1sld",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Because only one thing is green, the eye lands exactly where it should: the balance, a positive change, the next step. The restraint is what lets the data read before any decoration does."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "compass"
    },
    {
      "id": "8sh9ju45",
      "title": "The build",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "a87bc8um",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "wbstrktk",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "A system, not a screen"
              },
              {
                "id": "8zwt8vx4",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "I designed the whole journey a real product needs, not just a hero dashboard:"
              },
              {
                "id": "gjbu4vxq",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "A phone number and OTP access flow, with countdown and resend",
                  "A modular dashboard: balance, investment trend, outflow breakdown, upcoming bills, and biggest expense",
                  "An investments page with a performance graph, allocation, and a holdings table",
                  "A transactions page with filters and a categorized list",
                  "Full light and dark, across web, tablet, and mobile",
                  "A token and component library so every screen and both themes stay consistent"
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "0w8zbksl",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Designing the parts nobody notices, the tokens, the states, the second theme, is where an exercise stops being a mockup and starts being a product."
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "structure"
    },
