    {
      "id": "mzcnlh7c",
      "title": "The design system",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "bk4uomt4",
          "layout": "1-1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "zeyxra7i",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "Tokens, not guesswork"
              },
              {
                "id": "bltwrdth",
                "kind": "paragraph",
                "text": "Every value in Rasid is a token, so light and dark are the same components rather than two separate designs, and a new screen inherits the system instead of reinventing it."
              },
              {
                "id": "mlcgvmqc",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "Type: Inter, on a modular scale that holds up in English and Arabic",
                  "Colour: one emerald green (",
                  "#00C980) with a full green scale and neutrals, defined for light and dark",
                  "Tokens and local variables: colour, spacing, and radius, so theming is a switch, not a redraw",
                  "Components: buttons, inputs, tabs, charts, and cards, all built in auto layout"
                ]
              }
            ],
            [
              {
                "id": "rf409cxi",
                "kind": "image",
                "src": "/uploads/1784913934202-Design-System2.webp",
                "alt": "",
