      ],
      "icon": "layers"
    },
    {
      "id": "qxn4imrd",
      "title": "What I practiced",
      "rows": [
        {
          "id": "v37ga6ms",
          "layout": "1",
          "cells": [
            [
              {
                "id": "hfk83jx6",
                "kind": "heading",
                "level": 2,
                "text": "What I took from it"
              },
              {
                "id": "ft0k2hou",
                "kind": "list",
                "items": [
                  "System before screens. Building tokens and local variables first meant light and dark, and every new screen, came almost for free. The setup cost paid for itself by the second theme.",
                  "Holding one accent colour. Keeping green for action and positive change only, across a whole product, was harder and more useful than adding more colour would have been.",
                  "Designing data, not decorating it. A donut for the outflow split, an area chart for the balance trend, both kept to the green scale and neutrals, so the numbers read at a glance instead of fighting for attention.",
                  "Scoping honestly. I built the core flows and marked the rest, spending, notifications, profile, and the detail screens, as next, instead of half designing everything at once."
                ]
              }
            ]
          ]
        }
      ],
      "icon": "insight"
    },
